WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.175
Lesson 2.4.

00:00:02.175 --> 00:00:05.824
Impermanent loss & true LP P&L.

00:00:05.824 --> 00:00:07.775
By the end, you'll be able to

00:00:07.775 --> 00:00:10.572
calculate an LP position's full profit and

00:00:10.572 --> 00:00:13.304
loss, and judge it against simply holding.

00:00:14.604 --> 00:00:15.894
Here's the plan.

00:00:15.894 --> 00:00:18.479
First, what impermanent loss actually is,

00:00:18.479 --> 00:00:20.379
and the formula behind it.

00:00:20.379 --> 00:00:23.502
Second, a real worked example, calculating the

00:00:23.502 --> 00:00:26.394
full P&L, not just the headline number.

00:00:26.394 --> 00:00:28.545
And third, the checklist to run so

00:00:28.545 --> 00:00:31.064
you always know if LPing actually worked.

00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:35.682
Your L.P. position can show a twenty percent gain,

00:00:35.682 --> 00:00:38.584
and LPing can still have cost you money.

00:00:38.584 --> 00:00:41.728
Until you compare against simply holding the same tokens,

00:00:41.728 --> 00:00:44.059
you genuinely don't know which one is true.

00:00:45.359 --> 00:00:46.884
What impermanent loss is.

00:00:48.184 --> 00:00:50.820
Impermanent loss is how far your L.P.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.080
position lags simply holding the same starting

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:57.294
tokens, once their relative price changes.

00:00:57.294 --> 00:01:00.624
The formula: I.L. equals two times the square

00:01:00.624 --> 00:01:03.086
root of r, divided by one plus r,

00:01:03.086 --> 00:01:05.692
minus one, where r is the new price

00:01:05.692 --> 00:01:08.019
divided by your entry price.

00:01:08.019 --> 00:01:10.759
It's only impermanent if the price comes back.

00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:13.258
Withdraw after the move, and it's permanent,

00:01:13.258 --> 00:01:14.924
locked in the moment you exit.

00:01:16.224 --> 00:01:18.329
Here's that formula as a curve.

00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:22.184
At r = 1, price unchanged, IL is zero.

00:01:22.184 --> 00:01:25.165
Move the price either direction and IL grows,

00:01:25.165 --> 00:01:27.758
and it grows the same whether the price

00:01:27.758 --> 00:01:29.897
doubled or was cut in half — the

00:01:29.897 --> 00:01:32.789
formula doesn't care which way it moved.

00:01:32.789 --> 00:01:37.764
Double the price, and IL is about −5.7%.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.974
Triple it, and it's already past −13%.

00:01:42.274 --> 00:01:43.364
Quick check.

00:01:43.364 --> 00:01:45.614
E.T.H. doubles in price.

00:01:45.614 --> 00:01:48.274
What's the impermanent loss on a fifty-fifty pool?

00:01:52.694 --> 00:01:55.094
The answer: about negative five point

00:01:55.094 --> 00:01:57.494
seven percent, against simply holding.

00:01:58.794 --> 00:01:59.879
The full P&L.

00:02:01.179 --> 00:02:04.685
Full LP profit and loss equals your LP value,

00:02:04.685 --> 00:02:08.719
plus fees earned, plus any incentives, minus gas.

00:02:08.719 --> 00:02:11.834
Compare that whole total against simply holding the

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:15.489
same starting tokens, not against your original deposit.

00:02:15.489 --> 00:02:18.229
That second comparison is the only one that

00:02:18.229 --> 00:02:20.969
tells you whether LPing itself was worth it.

00:02:22.269 --> 00:02:24.264
Walk through a real deposit.

00:02:24.264 --> 00:02:27.853
You put in 1 ETH and 3,000

00:02:27.853 --> 00:02:32.939
USDC at $3,000 an ETH, $6,000 total.

00:02:32.939 --> 00:02:34.644
From here, two paths.

00:02:34.644 --> 00:02:37.719
Holding, your tokens just sit there, unchanged.

00:02:37.719 --> 00:02:40.916
LPing, the pool automatically rebalances your

00:02:40.916 --> 00:02:42.953
share as the price moves.

00:02:42.953 --> 00:02:45.479
Both paths land at the same finish line: a

00:02:45.479 --> 00:02:48.768
straight comparison of what each one was actually worth.

00:02:50.068 --> 00:02:51.833
Now the exact numbers.

00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:54.949
E.T.H. rises to four thousand dollars.

00:02:54.949 --> 00:02:58.115
The pool rebalances you to zero point eight six

00:02:58.115 --> 00:03:01.677
six E.T.H. and three thousand four hundred sixty four

00:03:01.677 --> 00:03:05.041
U.S.D.C. Your L.P. value: zero point eight six six

00:03:05.041 --> 00:03:08.998
times four thousand, plus three thousand four hundred sixty

00:03:08.998 --> 00:03:12.794
four, six thousand nine hundred twenty eight dollars.

00:03:12.794 --> 00:03:15.408
Holding instead would be worth four thousand

00:03:15.408 --> 00:03:18.729
plus three thousand, seven thousand dollars exactly.

00:03:18.729 --> 00:03:21.534
That's impermanent loss of seventy two dollars,

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.289
about negative one point oh three percent.

00:03:24.289 --> 00:03:27.184
Add fees earned, one hundred fifty dollars,

00:03:27.184 --> 00:03:29.948
minus twenty dollars gas: your L.P. total

00:03:29.948 --> 00:03:32.449
is seven thousand fifty eight dollars.

00:03:33.749 --> 00:03:36.404
Here's the same result, framed two ways.

00:03:36.404 --> 00:03:39.711
Against your starting $6,000, you're up

00:03:39.711 --> 00:03:42.409
$1,058, and that looks great.

00:03:42.409 --> 00:03:44.825
But almost all of that came from

00:03:44.825 --> 00:03:47.614
ETH simply rising, not from LPing.

00:03:47.614 --> 00:03:52.053
Against holding, the honest comparison, you're up just $58.

00:03:52.053 --> 00:03:54.739
A master judges the position on

00:03:54.739 --> 00:03:56.753
the $58, not the $1,058.

00:03:58.053 --> 00:03:59.143
Quick check.

00:03:59.143 --> 00:04:03.153
Your L.P. position is up twenty percent since deposit.

00:04:03.153 --> 00:04:04.698
Did LPing actually work?

00:04:09.118 --> 00:04:12.978
The answer: unknown, until you compare against simply holding.

00:04:12.978 --> 00:04:14.664
That twenty percent could be

00:04:14.664 --> 00:04:16.698
entirely the underlying price move.

00:04:17.998 --> 00:04:19.723
Last check for this section.

00:04:19.723 --> 00:04:22.112
When does impermanent loss become permanent?

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:29.033
The answer: the moment you withdraw while the

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:31.262
price ratio is different from your entry.

00:04:32.562 --> 00:04:34.157
Where this judgment goes wrong.

00:04:35.457 --> 00:04:37.626
Here's how people misjudge a position

00:04:37.626 --> 00:04:39.752
even after learning the formula.

00:04:39.752 --> 00:04:42.347
Watching the token count go up, and calling

00:04:42.347 --> 00:04:44.825
that a win, while ignoring what that same

00:04:44.825 --> 00:04:47.248
basket is actually worth in dollars.

00:04:47.248 --> 00:04:51.384
Forgetting incentive reward tokens entirely, extra emissions

00:04:51.384 --> 00:04:53.690
on top of swap fees, which change

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.753
the real total either way.

00:04:55.753 --> 00:04:59.084
Comparing against the wrong hold baseline, today's

00:04:59.084 --> 00:05:01.435
price of just one token, instead of

00:05:01.435 --> 00:05:04.543
the actual basket you originally deposited.

00:05:04.543 --> 00:05:08.131
And ignoring the gas cost of frequent compounding, which

00:05:08.131 --> 00:05:11.279
quietly eats the very fees it's meant to reinvest.

00:05:12.579 --> 00:05:14.054
Before you judge a position.

00:05:15.354 --> 00:05:18.944
Run this on every open L.P. position, weekly.

00:05:18.944 --> 00:05:22.664
Track P&L against holding, not against your deposit.

00:05:22.664 --> 00:05:26.224
Record impermanent loss, fees, incentives and gas as

00:05:26.224 --> 00:05:29.949
separate line items, never blended into one number.

00:05:29.949 --> 00:05:33.042
And set an exit rule: if fees consistently fail

00:05:33.042 --> 00:05:36.499
to cover impermanent loss, that position is done.

00:05:36.499 --> 00:05:39.646
Two calculator commands do this math for

00:05:39.646 --> 00:05:42.562
you directly: I.L. by ratio, and L.P.

00:05:42.562 --> 00:05:45.709
break-even by ratio, days, and fee A.P.R.

00:05:47.009 --> 00:05:49.224
Your turn, 5 to 10 minutes.

00:05:49.224 --> 00:05:52.183
Pull up one open LP position, yours or a

00:05:52.183 --> 00:05:55.154
real one you can see the numbers for.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:58.826
Calculate its full P&L against holding, not against the

00:05:58.826 --> 00:06:02.564
deposit, and write down what LPing itself actually added.

00:06:03.864 --> 00:06:07.285
To recap: impermanent loss is 2 times the square

00:06:07.285 --> 00:06:09.728
root of r, over 1 plus r, minus 1,

00:06:09.728 --> 00:06:13.169
and it's only impermanent until you withdraw.

00:06:13.169 --> 00:06:15.712
Full LP P&L is your LP value,

00:06:15.712 --> 00:06:19.064
plus fees and incentives, minus gas.

00:06:19.064 --> 00:06:21.599
And the only honest comparison is against

00:06:21.599 --> 00:06:24.194
holding, not against your original deposit.

00:06:25.494 --> 00:06:29.394
That's impermanent loss and true LP profit and loss.

00:06:29.394 --> 00:06:31.978
Next up, Lesson 2.5: MEV, and

00:06:31.978 --> 00:06:34.649
protecting your trades from it.
